1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,818
Evaluate an AI application at several layers.

2
00:00:02,968 --> 00:00:07,047
Unit tests check deterministic code such as authorization and loop limits.

3
00:00:07,197 --> 00:00:11,513
Adapter tests check request and response contracts over HTTP.

4
00:00:11,663 --> 00:00:15,386
Retrieval tests measure whether relevant authorized evidence is found.

5
00:00:15,536 --> 00:00:23,173
End-to-end evaluations measure task success, unsupported claims, appropriate abstention, latency, and cost.

6
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:29,541
Keep a versioned dataset containing normal requests, edge cases, adversarial inputs, and

7
00:00:29,541 --> 00:00:30,577
expected properties.

8
00:00:30,727 --> 00:00:35,015
Do not tune on the entire evaluation set; reserve holdout cases.

9
00:00:35,165 --> 00:00:38,492
A model grader can be useful but may share the same biases

10
00:00:38,492 --> 00:00:40,433
or mistakes as the model under test.

11
00:00:40,583 --> 00:00:43,880
Calibrate it against human judgments and report disagreement.

12
00:00:44,030 --> 00:00:47,845
The supplied JUnit suite proves that unknown tools are rejected and another

13
00:00:47,845 --> 00:00:49,116
tenant’s order is hidden.

14
00:00:49,266 --> 00:00:52,863
It does not prove that an arbitrary local model gives good answers.

15
00:00:53,013 --> 00:00:56,949
Run the same support questions through scripted mode and live mode, record

16
00:00:56,949 --> 00:01:00,886
the model version and prompt hash, and compare evidence support rather than

17
00:01:00,886 --> 00:01:01,542
wording alone.

18
00:01:01,692 --> 00:01:07,627
Build a CSV with 30 cases and columns for tool accuracy, groundedness,

19
00:01:07,627 --> 00:01:11,089
access violations, calls, elapsed milliseconds, and tokens.

20
00:01:11,239 --> 00:01:14,300
Define a release threshold before running the experiment.

21
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:18,384
Treat any access violation as a release blocker rather than averaging it

22
00:01:18,384 --> 00:01:18,711
away.

23
00:01:18,861 --> 00:01:24,120
Report task success with numerator and denominator, and keep cost and latency

24
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:24,558
distributions.

25
00:01:24,708 --> 00:01:29,164
A threshold such as 90 percent success is a project choice, not

26
00:01:29,164 --> 00:01:30,649
a universal industry standard.

27
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:31,471
Question.

28
00:01:31,621 --> 00:01:34,235
Why is exact string matching often inadequate?

29
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:34,962
Answer.

30
00:01:35,112 --> 00:01:40,269
Several phrasings can express the same supported answer; compare required facts and

31
00:01:40,269 --> 00:01:41,129
prohibited behavior.

32
00:01:41,279 --> 00:01:41,950
Question.

33
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,332
What does a mocked model test establish?

34
00:01:44,482 --> 00:01:45,059
Answer.

35
00:01:45,209 --> 00:01:50,391
It establishes orchestration behavior for supplied decisions, not the quality of real

36
00:01:50,391 --> 00:01:51,255
model decisions.
